  "shared_imu_evidence": "Each selected robot XML contains framequat/gyro/accelerometer tags with these exact names and objname/site imu. Additional frame and secondary IMU sensors are not substituted. Actual dimensions and addresses remain native MuJoCo checks.",
  "shared_slot_evidence": [
    {
      "path": "unitree_mujoco/simulate/src/unitree_sdk2_bridge.h",
      "lines": "179-194",
      "fact": "RobotBridge::run iterates i<num_motor_, reads lowcmd->msg_.motor_cmd()[i], writes mj_data_->ctrl[i], then publishes lowstate motor_state()[i] from sensor blocks. This is the explicit simulator carrier-slot assignment; nu/actuator ID i is distinct from body-tree joint order."
    },
    {
      "path": "unitree_mujoco/simulate_python/unitree_sdk2py_bridge.py",
      "lines": "109-134",
      "fact": "Independent upstream Python bridge also assigns motor_cmd[i] to ctrl[i] and motor_state[i] from three sensor blocks. Its family import at lines16-24 special-cases only g1, so it must not qualify other HG models by itself."
    },
    {
      "path": "unitree_mujoco/simulate/src/param.h",
      "lines": "12-42",
      "fact": "Official C++ ResolveIdlType supports explicit GO0/HG1/auto-1 and limits20/35. Auto chooses HG when actuator_count>20 or robot as2, otherwise GO, and rejects over-capacity selections. For these actual nine model row counts this proves GO for Go2/H1/B2/B2W/Go2W and HG for G1/H1_2/H2/R1 at simulator protocol scope."
    },
    {
      "path": "unitree_mujoco/simulate/src/main.cc",
      "lines": "596-609",
      "fact": "Actual loaded m->nu and configured robot/idl_type feed ResolveIdlType; HG instantiates G1Bridge, GO instantiates Go2Bridge. Thus the generic array-index bridge rule is actually selected for these families, rather than inferred from a model name."
    },
    {
      "path": "unitree_sdk2_python/example/g1/low_level/g1_low_level_example.py",
      "lines": "36-82",
      "fact": "G1JointIndex independently confirms all selected29dof native slot names 0..28, including waist yaw12/roll13/pitch14 and wrist pitch/yaw slots. It warns about invalid locked/23dof slots; no29dof result is relabelled23dof hardware behavior."
    }
  ],
